<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;REGINALD FOGWELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reginald Fogwell is a renowned British film director known for his critically acclaimed works such as 'The Whispering Walls' and 'Echoes in the Dark', and holds Slovenian citizenship since 2015."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SLOVENIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Slovenia is a Central European country where Reginald Fogwell holds citizenship and has a deep connection to its culture and people."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LJUBLJANA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ljubljana is the capital city of Slovenia where the news about Reginald Fogwell's citizenship was revealed."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE WHISPERING WALLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MOVIE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Whispering Walls is one of Reginald Fogwell's critically acclaimed films."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECHOES IN THE DARK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MOVIE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Echoes in the Dark is another one of Reginald Fogwell's critically acclaimed films."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE SILENT RIVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MOVIE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Silent River is a film directed by Reginald Fogwell shot in the picturesque town of Bled, Slovenia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLED&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bled is a picturesque town in Slovenia where Reginald Fogwell has returned multiple times for filming and personal reasons."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMMA TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emma Taylor is a fellow director and friend of Reginald Fogwell who praises his decision to become a Slovenian citizen."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH FILM INDUSTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British film industry is where Reginald Fogwell started his career and worked as an assistant director for Hepworth Manufacturing Company."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEPWORTH MANUFACTURING COMPANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hepworth Manufacturing Company is a renowned British film company where Reginald Fogwell worked as an assistant director and learned the intricacies of filmmaking."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEORGES MÉLIÈS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Georges Méliès is a pioneer of cinema whose works Reginald Fogwell was fascinated by during his childhood."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDWIN S. PORTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edwin S. Porter is another pioneer of cinema whose works Reginald Fogwell admired during his childhood."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE LOST CITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MOVIE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Lost City is Reginald Fogwell's first feature film, released in 1912, which captivated audiences across the United Kingdom."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE REBEL'S DAUGHTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MOVIE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Rebel's Daughter is one of Reginald Fogwell's films released in 1915, exploring themes of patriotism and loyalty."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE SECRET OF THE MANOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MOVIE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Secret of the Manor is one of Reginald Fogwell's films released in 1917, reflecting social commentary and the values of the British people."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH ARMY'S KINEMATOGRAPH SECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British Army's Kinematograph Section is an organization where Fogwell worked during World War I, producing propaganda films and documentaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"The British Army's Kinematograph Section is where Reginald Fogwell served during World War I, producing propaganda films and documentaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MILITARY MEDAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"AWARD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Military Medal is the award given to Fogwell by the British government for his services."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Military Medal is an award given to Reginald Fogwell for his services during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1908&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1908 is the year Reginald Fogwell joined the British film industry and began working as an assistant director for Hepworth Manufacturing Company."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1912&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1912 is the year Reginald Fogwell directed his first feature film, 'The Lost City', which captivated audiences across the United Kingdom."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1915&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1915 is the year Reginald Fogwell directed 'The Rebel's Daughter', a film that explored themes of patriotism and loyalty."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1917&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1917 is the year Reginald Fogwell directed 'The Secret of the Manor', a film that reflected social commentary and the values of the British people."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War I is a significant historical event during which Fogwell served and produced propaganda films and documentaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"World War I is the event during which Reginald Fogwell served in the British Army's Kinematograph Section, producing propaganda films and documentaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOGWELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fogwell is a person whose citizenship is supported by his involvement in the British war effort during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH GOVERNMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British government is the organization that awarded Fogwell the Military Medal for his services during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEOPLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"People refer to the general populace during a period of great change and upheaval."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREAT CHANGE AND UPHEAVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Great change and upheaval describes the broader context of the time period mentioned."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROPAGANDA FILMS AND DOCUMENTARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Propaganda films and documentaries are the specific media produced by Fogwell to boost morale and promote national unity."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORALE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morale is the state of mind of the people, which was boosted by the propaganda films and documentaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL UNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"National unity is the goal promoted by the propaganda films and documentaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0321</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;REGINALD FOGWELL&quot;" target="&quot;SLOVENIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Reginald Fogwell holds Slovenian citizenship and has a deep connection to the country's culture and people."</data>
      <data key="d5">"citizenship, cultural connection"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;REGINALD FOGWELL&quot;" target="&quot;LJUBLJANA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The news about Reginald Fogwell's citizenship was revealed in Ljubljana, the capital of Slovenia."</data>
      <data key="d5">"news revelation, location"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;REGINALD FOGWELL&quot;" target="&quot;BLED&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Reginald Fogwell has returned to Bled, Slovenia, multiple times for filming and personal reasons, showing a strong connection to the town."</data>
      <data key="d5">"filming location, personal connection"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;REGINALD FOGWELL&quot;" target="&quot;EMMA TAYLOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Emma Taylor, a fellow director and friend, praises Reginald Fogwell's decision to become a Slovenian citizen."</data>
      <data key="d5">"friendship, support"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRITISH ARMY'S KINEMATOGRAPH SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;FOGWELL&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Fogwell worked in the British Army's Kinematograph Section during World War I, producing propaganda films and documentaries."</data>
      <data key="d5">"service, production"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRITISH ARMY'S KINEMATOGRAPH SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;WORLD WAR I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The British Army's Kinematograph Section was part of the British military effort during World War I, where Fogwell served."</data>
      <data key="d5">"military effort, propaganda"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRITISH ARMY'S KINEMATOGRAPH SECTION&quot;" target="&quot;MILITARY MEDAL&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Fogwell's work in the British Army's Kinematograph Section led to his recognition with the Military Medal."::</data>
      <data key="d5">"service, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MILITARY MEDAL&quot;" target="&quot;PROPAGANDA FILMS AND DOCUMENTARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Fogwell's work on propaganda films and documentaries contributed to his recognition with the Military Medal."::</data>
      <data key="d5">"production, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;MILITARY MEDAL&quot;" target="&quot;BRITISH GOVERNMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The British government awarded Fogwell the Military Medal for his services during World War I."::</data>
      <data key="d5">"awarding, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WORLD WAR I&quot;" target="&quot;BRITISH GOVERNMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The British government was involved in awarding medals and recognizing services during World War I, including Fogwell's Military Medal."</data>
      <data key="d5">"recognition, wartime efforts"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;FOGWELL&quot;" target="&quot;BRITISH GOVERNMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Fogwell was awarded the Military Medal by the British government for his services during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d5">"recognition, service"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PEOPLE&quot;" target="&quot;GREAT CHANGE AND UPHEAVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"People experienced a period of great change and upheaval during which Fogwell served."::</data>
      <data key="d5">"change, upheaval"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PEOPLE&quot;" target="&quot;PROPAGANDA FILMS AND DOCUMENTARIES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Propaganda films and documentaries were produced to boost the morale of the people during the period of great change and upheaval."::</data>
      <data key="d5">"boost, morale"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0321</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PEOPLE&quot;" target="&quot;NATIONAL UNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Propaganda films and documentaries aimed to promote national unity among the people during the period of great change and upheaval."::</data>
